  "facts": [
    "The Oslofjord Tunnel, opened 29 June 2000, stretches 7,306 meters beneath the fjord, plunging to 134 meters below sea level and featuring a seven‑percent gradient that necessitates a dedicated climbing lane.",
    "After flooding in 2003 and 2008, the tunnel’s emergency design includes 25 pressurized evacuation rooms, each capable of sheltering thirty to fifty people while firefighting crews battle sea‑water ingress.",
    "Tolling began in 2000 with a manual plaza, switched to automated Autopass in 2014, and was abolished entirely on 30 August 2016, making the tunnel free for all traffic today."
